# Leapfrog Boot Instructions — Team 10

This is an agent-agnostic project memory spine. `AGENTS.md` and `DELIVERY.md` are mandatory for every coding agent; use the same rules in other chat-based tools.

## Boot

1. Read root `AGENTS.md`, `DELIVERY.md`, and `agent-governance.md`.
2. Read `.leapfrog/index.md` and the latest x/v checkpoint pair listed there.
3. Read the last five entries of `.leapfrog/log.md` and `.leapfrog/wiki/hot.md`.
4. Read only the active track(s) and `.leapfrog/board.md` tasks relevant to the assigned work.
5. State what changed, what was verified, what not to retry blindly, and which task/files you own. Start chat responses with `Team10-LetzGo!`.

## Checkpoint rules

- Write both x (what exists) and v (what is moving) files using a shared sequence, e.g. `cp-001-x.md` and `cp-001-v.md`.
- Update the pair every two hours during active work, after material decisions/interface changes, before handoff/context compaction, and at session end.
- Update `.leapfrog/index.md`, `.leapfrog/wiki/hot.md`, relevant track files, and append to `.leapfrog/log.md` whenever a checkpoint is created.
- Logs are append-only. Keep old checkpoints; never silently rewrite prior state. Correct errors with a new entry and link to it.
- Capture verification as observed evidence. Do not write “passed” when a check was not run.

## Current operating mode

- Layer 1 checkpoints and coordination board are active.
- Layer 2 is limited to a concise hot cache and source/decision notes as needed; do not create a large wiki until there is material to preserve.
- Layer 3 harness evolution is not active; there are not yet enough project traces to justify it.

